      "id": 1,
      "text": "Fort Gratiot Lighthouse, built in 1814, was named after engineer General Charles Gratiot and guarded the junction of Lake Huron and the St. Clair River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.americanheritage.com/content/fort-gratiot-lighthouse",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The lighthouse’s white brick tower rose 74 feet at first, then was extended to 86 feet in the early 1860s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.americanheritage.com/content/fort-gratiot-lighthouse",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fort Gratiot Township was officially established in 1867, following the fort’s military use between 1814 and 1879.",
